    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 12&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;c530a62b-adf4-4b9e-b6c2-c629aca6323b&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;c530a62b-adf4-4b9e-b6c2-c629aca6323b&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hutVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 13&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;f01971c9-80d7-44ab-ae7a-95424ae5ed0f&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;f01971c9-80d7-44ab-ae7a-95424ae5ed0f&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;R2nVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;pa.PhysicalComponent&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;CMOS Backup Battery Holder&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;userSpecificInput:ReqContents&quot;: &quot;&lt;h1>CMOS Backup Battery Holder&lt;/h1>\n\n&lt;p>A CMOS backup battery holder is a component used in electronic devices to provide backup power for the CMOS (Complementary Metal-Oxide-Semiconductor) memory. The CMOS memory is responsible for storing and maintaining important system settings and configurations even when the main power supply is disconnected or unavailable.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>The backup battery holder is typically a small and compact device that houses a replaceable coin cell battery. It is designed to ensure a reliable and uninterrupted power supply to the CMOS memory, preventing data loss or corruption during power interruptions or when the device is turned off. The battery holder is often integrated into the motherboard or PCB (Printed Circuit Board) design of the electronic device.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>Commonly used batteries in CMOS backup battery holders are CR2032 lithium coin cell batteries, known for their long shelf life, low self-discharge rate, and stable voltage output. These batteries provide sufficient power to maintain the data in the CMOS memory for an extended period, typically several years.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>CMOS backup battery holders feature a secure and easy-to-use mechanism for battery insertion and replacement. They are designed to protect the battery from accidental short circuits or physical damage. The holders generally have a positive and negative terminal or contacts to establish a proper electrical connection with the battery.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>References:&lt;/p>\n&lt;ol>\n  &lt;li>Smith, T. (2020). &lt;i>The Basics of CMOS Battery Replacement on a Computer Motherboard&lt;/i>. Lifewire. [Online]. Available: &lt;a href=\&quot;https://www.lifewire.com/cmos-battery-replacement-on-a-desktop-pc-motherboard-2618161\&quot;>https://www.lifewire.com/cmos-battery-replacement-on-a-desktop-pc-motherboard-2618161&lt;/a>&lt;/li>\n  &lt;li>Morales, J. (2018). &lt;i>How Does a CMOS Battery Work in a Computer?&lt;/i> ThoughtCo. [Online]. Available: &lt;a href=\&quot;https://www.thoughtco.com/what-is-cmos-battery-2618162\&quot;>https://www.thoughtco.com/what-is-cmos-battery-2618162&lt;/a>&lt;/li>\n&lt;/ol>&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;c6924851-77c6-47f5-8073-964aa967c2cb&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;c6924851-77c6-47f5-8073-964aa967c2cb&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hDlVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;xqpVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;pa.PhysicalComponent&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;USB 2&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;0657e1d7-ea63-40cf-898c-3432d390ea93&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;0657e1d7-ea63-40cf-898c-3432d390ea93&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RrnVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;xSrVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 1&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;af3ac2ad-6577-4fde-82b5-b428c62a7d35&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;af3ac2ad-6577-4fde-82b5-b428c62a7d35&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RuhVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 2&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;34a9d53c-36da-4b37-9b5f-b100046a2031&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;34a9d53c-36da-4b37-9b5f-b100046a2031&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hapVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-