net&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;c007edb2-f0c2-41a9-988f-39efb48c7278&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;c007edb2-f0c2-41a9-988f-39efb48c7278&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RPtVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;h6hVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 1&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;45cea6c4-a3c4-4b0c-9199-6f99f18ff750&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;45cea6c4-a3c4-4b0c-9199-6f99f18ff750&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;ROpVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 2&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;c7bd574b-249f-486c-9ced-bbee296fdfda&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;c7bd574b-249f-486c-9ced-bbee296fdfda&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;halVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;pa.PhysicalComponent&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;COM&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;2ad91d18-9c2b-4639-9a6d-956b4681518f&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;2ad91d18-9c2b-4639-9a6d-956b4681518f&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RntVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;xShVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 1&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;39004d9f-af48-453d-9f97-598e000892cd&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;39004d9f-af48-453d-9f97-598e000892cd&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;ButVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 2&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;60ff4cf1-6849-4467-bc2b-413307710aa4&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;60ff4cf1-6849-4467-bc2b-413307710aa4&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RipVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;pa.PhysicalComponent&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;HDMI Connector&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;userSpecificInput:ReqContents&quot;: &quot;&lt;title>&lt;/title>\n&lt;p>HDMI Connector&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>A High Definition Multimedia Interface (HDMI) connector is a digital audio/video interface commonly used to connect various devices such as televisions, monitors, projectors, and audio/video receivers. It allows the transmission of high-quality uncompressed audio and video signals in a single cable, providing a convenient and efficient way to connect devices without sacrificing signal quality.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>The HDMI connector typically consists of 19 pins, which carry both digital audio and video signals. It supports various video resolutions, including standard definition (480i/p), high definition (720p/1080i), and ultra-high definition (4K/8K). HDMI also supports advanced audio formats, such as Dolby TrueHD and DTS-HD Master Audio, providing a superior audio experience.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>One of the key advantages of HDMI is its ability to transmit digital signals without degradation, resulting in a better overall picture and sound quality compared to analog connections. It also supports features like Consumer Electronics Control (CEC), which allows the control of multiple devices through a single remote, and Audio Return Channel (ARC), which enables audio to be sent upstream from a television to an audio device without the need for a separate audio cable.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>References:&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>HDMI Specification 2.1&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>Techopedia - High Definition Multimedia Interface (HDMI)&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>\n&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;ed44a72b-1f04-4963-84fb-42e355df82e4&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;ed44a72b-1f04-4963-84fb-42e355df82e4&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RjhVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;xKlVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 1&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;431532a0-65f9-458e-bbbf-32d515edd58b&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;431532a0-65f9-458e-bbbf-32d515edd58b&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;henVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 2&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;1dab628d-ff99-4ebb-bdbf-253d2b3c0294&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;1dab628d-ff99-4ebb-bdbf-253d2b3c0294&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RCrVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;pa.PhysicalComponent&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;HDD drive&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;userSpecificInput:ReqContents&quot;: &quot;&lt;title>&lt;/title>\n&lt;p>HDD Drive Description&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>An HDD (Hard Disk Drive) is a data storage device that uses magnetic storage to store and retrieve digital information. It consists of one or more rigid disks coated with a magnetic material and rotating at high speeds, while an actuator arm with read/write heads moves across the rotating disks to access and modify data.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>HDD drives are commonly used in desktop and laptop computers, servers, and external storage devices due to their large storage capacity and relatively lower cost compared to other storage options. They are capable of storing various types of data, including documents, images, videos, and software.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>One of the key advantages of HDD drives is their ability to retain data even when the power is turned off, making them a reliable long-term storage option. However, their mechanical components make them susceptible to damage from physical shocks and vibrations, potentially leading to data loss or drive failure.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>For more detailed information on HDD drives, please refer to the following references:&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>&amp;quot;Hard Disk Drive&amp;quot; - Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_disk_drive&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>&amp;quot;The History of the Hard Drive&amp;quot; - PCMag. https://www.pcmag.com/news/the-history-of-the-hard-drive&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>&amp;quot;How Hard Disks Work&amp;quot; - HowStuffWorks. https://www.howstuffworks.com/hard-disk-drive.htm&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>\n&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;f68d202f-10d6-43a1-8e13-27d12f968994&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;f68d202f-10d6-43a1-8e13-27d12f968994&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RXlVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;h_pVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 1&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;99031c87-c0c0-4e1d-8208-82470ab5c9dc&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;99031c87-c0c0-4e1d-8208-82470ab5c9dc&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;R2hVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 2&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;2f95073c-32a9-4c02-91ad-510606ed188d&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;2f95073c-32a9-4c02-91ad-510606ed188d&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hyhVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;pa.PhysicalComponent&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PCIe Card Adapter&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;30053e97-94e1-4428-9a9e-1406e44e27e9&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;30053e97-94e1-4428-9a9e-1406e44e27e9&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hLlVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;xypVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 1&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;21839015-1284-4013-a7bd-0dda0a5a4f2c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;21839015-1284-4013-a7bd-0dda0a5a4f2c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;havVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 2&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;079cd771-1b3f-48d1-a090-74cbe07101cc&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;079cd771-1b3f-48d1-a090-74cbe07101cc&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hGhVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 3&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;cccaf7c0-3eff-4e8e-80c6-97f0339e3de6&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;cccaf7c0-3eff-4e8e-80c6-97f0339e3de6&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;RepVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 4&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;f2554736-2170-4719-a1b4-b919fadc11c1&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;f2554736-2170-4719-a1b4-b919fadc11c1&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hetVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;pa.PhysicalComponent&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PCIe Card&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;userSpecificInput:ReqContents&quot;: &quot;&lt;meta charset=\&quot;UTF-8\&quot;>&lt;meta name=\&quot;viewport\&quot; content=\&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\&quot;>\n&lt;title>&lt;/title>\n&lt;p>PCIe Card&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>A PCIe card, also known as a Peripheral Component Interconnect Express card, is a hardware component that can be plugged into a computer&amp;#39;s PCIe slot to provide additional functionality or expand the capabilities of the system. PCIe is a high-speed serial bus standard used for connecting various devices to a computer&amp;#39;s motherboard.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>The PCIe card fits into one of the available expansion slots on the motherboard, providing a connection point for the card&amp;#39;s electronic circuitry to communicate with the computer&amp;#39;s CPU and other components. These cards can support a variety of functions, such as adding additional USB ports, network connectivity, sound cards, graphics processing units (GPUs), solid-state drives (SSDs), and more.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>The PCIe standard offers various versions, with each version providing increased bandwidth and improved performance compared to its predecessors. Some popular PCIe versions include PCIe 1.0/1.1, PCIe 2.0, PCIe 3.0, and the latest PCIe 4.0, which boasts higher data transfer speeds.&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>References:&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>PCI Express. (n.d.). Retrieved from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PCI_Express&lt;/p>\n\n&lt;p>PCIe vs. PCI: What&amp;#39;s the Difference? (2020, February 6). Retrieved from https://www.lifewire.com/pcie-vs-pci-4681867&lt;/p>\n&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Nature&quot;: &quot;NODE&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isHuman&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;isActor&quot;: &quot;false&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;Kind&quot;: &quot;UNSET&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;7e262398-5993-4344-8962-386f35e53221&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUmlID&quot;: &quot;7e262398-5993-4344-8962-386f35e53221&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;plmPk&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;tcuid&quot;: &quot;hHhVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;stableTcId&quot;: &quot;xulVRRlZ4nxmPD&quot;&#xA;      }&#xA;    },&#xA;    {&#xA;      &quot;projectID&quot;: &quot;f1c15a43-c4db-4988-ad6b-425ac13c834c&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;properties&quot;: {&#xA;        &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;PP 1&quot;,&#xA;        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;cs.PhysicalPort&quot;&#xA;      },&#xA;      &quot;umlID&quot;: &quot;07e1c5e3-e80b-4422-b0dd-12abfbbca609&quot;,&#xA;      &quot;fullUml