        <ownedSystemComponents xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.ctx:SystemComponent"
            id="9403fa3a-94ce-4cee-851f-d487c9359596" name="Industrial PC" description="&lt;title>&lt;/title>&#xA;&lt;p>Industrial PC Description&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>An Industrial PC, also known as an IPC, is a specialized computer system designed to withstand harsh operating conditions in industrial environments. It is specifically built to handle demanding applications and continuous operation in industries such as manufacturing, automation, oil and gas, transportation, and more.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Industrial PCs are built to be rugged, reliable, and durable, with features that allow them to function optimally in extreme temperatures, high humidity, dust, vibrations, and other challenging conditions. They are typically enclosed in robust casings or chassis for protection against environmental factors and to meet industry-specific requirements.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>These computers are equipped with powerful hardware components to ensure high performance and efficiency. The processors used in industrial PCs are generally industrial-grade, capable of handling complex tasks and multitasking effectively. They also come with ample memory, storage, and expansion options to accommodate specialized software and support data-intensive applications.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Moreover, industrial PCs often have multiple I/O ports and interfaces to facilitate connectivity with various devices, sensors, and machinery typically found in industrial settings. These interfaces may include Ethernet, RS232/485 serial ports, USB, VGA/HDMI for video output, and more.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Overall, Industrial PCs play a vital role in automation, control, monitoring, and data acquisition in industrial environments. They are designed to ensure stability, reliability, and longevity in demanding industrial applications, providing a dependable computing solution for critical operations.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>References:&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Han, Y., &amp;amp; Liu, C. (2020). Industrial PC. In Encyclopedia of Electrical and Electronics Engineering (pp. 1-8). CRC Press.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Industrial PC - an overview. (n.d.). ScienceDirect. Retrieved from https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/industrial-pc&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Industrial Computer - Industrial PC, Rugged computer - Concepts and Benefits. (n.d.). Eurotech. Retrieved from https://www.eurotech.com/en/products/industrial-pc&lt;/p>&#xA;"
            appliedPropertyValueGroups="#bb55aee8-b352-4c32-aa42-832682c825f5">
          <ownedExtensions xsi:type="smw:TcItemRevision" id="80380aa0-cee5-48a7-9039-4d24d81e1c59"
              tcuid="QalZTqJ74nxmPD" stableTcId="AWlZTqJ74nxmPD" itemId="167235" revisionId="A"/>
          <ownedConstraints xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.capellacore:Constraint"
              id="3e19b6ff-d668-4027-9333-0f267999348e" name="" constrainedElements="#9403fa3a-94ce-4cee-851f-d487c9359596">
